# Line endings — declared, not inherited.
#
# Without this file the checkout depends on each machine's `core.autocrlf`.
# On the owner's Windows box that setting is `true`, which expanded LF to CRLF
# on checkout; every file that has since been rewritten by an editor came back
# as LF, so the tree drifted into a mix — `index.html` was the last CRLF holdout
# among the nine deployed pages while its eight peers were already LF.
#
# Git normalises to LF in the object database either way, so this changes
# nothing about what is committed. What it fixes is the WORKING TREE and, more
# to the point, `dist/`: `scripts/build/dist.js` copies raw bytes, so a CRLF
# checkout shipped a file that differed byte-for-byte from an LF checkout of the
# same commit. Deploy output should not depend on who ran the build.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch the bytes, never try to diff them as text.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.jfif   binary
*.webp   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.mp4    binary
*.webm   binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.zip    binary
*.exe    binary
*.psd    binary
*.ai     binary

# Committed build artefacts. Generated by `npm run build`, never hand-edited —
# collapsing them in diffs keeps a bundle refresh from burying the source change
# that caused it. They are still fully version-controlled.
app.js      -diff linguist-generated
tallal.js   -diff linguist-generated
